
<div class="history-section py-5">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="text-center">History of the Election Commission of Pakistan</h2>
        <p class="text-center">The Election Commission of Pakistan (ECP) was established in 1956 under the Constitution of Pakistan. It is an autonomous body that oversees the electoral process in Pakistan. The ECP ensures free, fair, and transparent elections, managing the voter registration, delimitation of constituencies, and the organization of elections for the national, provincial, and local assemblies. Over the years, the ECP has played a pivotal role in maintaining the democratic process and ensuring that the citizens of Pakistan have a voice in the governance of the country.</p>
    </div>
</div>

